1. Private Access Modifier
The private access modifier is specified using the keyword private. The methods or data members declared as private are accessible only within the class in which they are declared.
- Provides the highest level of restriction.
- Commonly used to protect fields and implementation details.
class Person {
    // private variable
    private String name;
    public void setName(String name)  {
        this.name = name; // accessible within class
    }
    public String getName() { return name; }
}
public class Geeks {
    public static void main(String[] args)

String getName() { return name; }
}
public class Geeks {
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        Person p = new Person();
        p.setName("Alice");
        // System.out.println(p.name); // Error: 'name'
        // has private access
        System.out.println(p.getName());
    }
}
Output
Alice
Explanation: Direct access to name is not allowed outside Person, enforcing encapsulation.
